Elf2Mac: handle cross-section jump-table references instead of aborting

NetHack keeps function-pointer tables in .data (windowprocs, sound
interface, ...).  Each entry is a relocation from .data into a code
section; upstream Elf2Mac asserts that jump-table relocations stay
within their own section and aborts the link.  Treat the cross-section
case as a regular jump-table relocation.

Not yet merged upstream (checked against autc04/Retro68 master,
2026-06).  Apply to the Retro68 source tree and rebuild Elf2Mac; no
other component of the toolchain needs patching or rebuilding.

diff --git a/Elf2Mac/Section.cc b/Elf2Mac/Section.cc
index eb0097cbf9..2842deda14 100644
--- a/Elf2Mac/Section.cc
+++ b/Elf2Mac/Section.cc
@@ -229,13 +229,11 @@ void Section::FixRelocs(bool allowDirectCodeRefs)
                     {
                         if(sym.section.get() != this)
                         {
-                            std::cerr << "Invalid ref from "
-                                      << name << ":" << std::hex << rela.r_offset-shdr.sh_addr << std::dec
-                                      << " to " << sym.section->name
-                                      << "(" << sym.name << ")"
-                                      << "+" << rela.r_offset << std::endl;
+                            /* Cross-section JT ref with addend (e.g. function
+                               pointer in .data referencing .code).
+                               Treat as a regular relocation instead of aborting. */
+                            relocBase = RelocBase::jumptable;
                         }
-                        assert(sym.section.get() == this);
                     }
                 }
                 else if(allowDirectCodeRefs)
